WEBVTT

00:00:00.020 --> 00:00:04.650
<b>Shiisaka Shirasawa Tunnel</b>

00:00:05.210 --> 00:00:06.810
The lead pack is here!

00:00:06.810 --> 00:00:08.770
It's Hakone Academy and Kyoto Fushimi!

00:00:08.770 --> 00:00:10.690
That's #14, the guy from the sprint!

00:00:10.690 --> 00:00:13.400
#116 has rejoined his team, too!

00:00:13.400 --> 00:00:15.460
There's one Sohoku rider with them!

00:00:15.460 --> 00:00:17.030
It's the red guy!

00:00:24.920 --> 00:00:32.510
<b><i>Yowamushi Pedal</i></b>

00:01:51.810 --> 00:01:56.320
<i>LINE.16  Sohoku Falls Behind</i>

00:01:54.870 --> 00:01:58.520
<i>It's suddenly muggy. The air's hot.</i>

00:01:58.520 --> 00:02:01.010
<i>The temperature rose sharply 
once we exited the tunnel.</i>

00:02:01.730 --> 00:02:04.180
<i>Our elevation must have 
decreased quite a bit.</i>

00:02:04.750 --> 00:02:07.690
<i>Once this downhill ends, we'll be in Numata.</i>

00:02:08.300 --> 00:02:10.860
<i>From there, the road will 
be flat for a while.</i>

00:02:10.860 --> 00:02:13.730
<i>But once that ends,
 we'll enter the mountains.</i>

00:02:14.330 --> 00:02:19.030
<i>Naturally, since I'm a genius, I won't let 
Hakone Academy or Kyoto Fushimi get away.</i>

00:02:19.950 --> 00:02:23.740
<i>But honestly, having to do all of it 
myself puts me at a disadvantage.</i>

00:02:30.850 --> 00:02:32.020
<i>Damn!</i>

00:02:32.020 --> 00:02:34.390
<i>Kyoto Fushimi's staggering their line</i>

00:02:34.390 --> 00:02:36.550
<i>and moving around so I can't get 
out of the wind behind them.</i>

00:02:37.550 --> 00:02:40.090
<i>Is this one of Midousuji's phases?</i>

00:02:40.870 --> 00:02:42.350
<i>They're absolutely right.</i>

00:02:42.350 --> 00:02:46.020
<i>If I want to get out of the wind, I should
 go get some of my own teammates.</i>

00:02:46.650 --> 00:02:50.520
<i>Right now, I'm just an eyesore. 
They won't cooperate with me.</i>

00:02:52.150 --> 00:02:55.940
<i>My legs are starting to feel modestly 
exhausted from this modest attack.</i>

00:02:56.990 --> 00:03:00.130
<i>No, wait. I'm a genius.</i>

00:03:00.130 --> 00:03:02.240
<i>I can handle this myself.</i>

00:03:03.100 --> 00:03:05.300
<i>I won't let modesty beat me!</i>

00:03:06.210 --> 00:03:07.040
<i>But...</i>

00:03:07.970 --> 00:03:10.960
<i>It would be easier if they caught up.</i>

00:03:12.020 --> 00:03:13.540
<i>My team...</i>

00:03:14.670 --> 00:03:15.860
<i>Onoda-kun...</i>

00:03:16.300 --> 00:03:17.420
<i>Teshima-san...</i>

00:03:18.180 --> 00:03:19.590
<i>Hotshot!</i>

00:03:20.540 --> 00:03:21.510
<i>Come on!</i>

00:03:22.070 --> 00:03:23.220
<i>Catch up!</i>

00:03:28.510 --> 00:03:30.240
This is hopeless.

00:03:30.240 --> 00:03:32.140
Teshima-san, I'll switch with you.

00:03:33.150 --> 00:03:34.520
Thanks, Onoda.

00:03:34.520 --> 00:03:38.320
We'll catch up to the front somehow.

00:03:39.340 --> 00:03:41.380
<i>Our situation couldn't be worse.</i>

00:03:41.380 --> 00:03:43.990
<i>We're pretty far behind the front.</i>

00:03:44.660 --> 00:03:49.110
<i>I wish we could catch up,
 but they're six plus six plus one.</i>

00:03:49.740 --> 00:03:53.020
<i>That's thirteen riders. There's only three of us.</i>

00:03:53.020 --> 00:03:56.210
<i>And one of us is a climber who 
won't be good on the flats.</i>

00:03:56.210 --> 00:03:59.210
<b>Feed Zone</b>

00:03:57.090 --> 00:03:59.210
<i>At the feed zone earlier...</i>

00:03:59.210 --> 00:04:00.420
Teshima-san!

00:04:00.420 --> 00:04:01.420
Onoda-san!

00:04:01.420 --> 00:04:02.930
Thank you!

00:04:03.450 --> 00:04:07.350
Teshima-san, you're five minutes 
and ten seconds behind the front!

00:04:08.560 --> 00:04:11.020
I-It's okay!

00:04:11.020 --> 00:04:13.190
I-I'm sure you can catch up!

00:04:13.640 --> 00:04:15.460
Please catch up!

00:04:15.460 --> 00:04:19.560
Sohoku, go!

00:04:18.210 --> 00:04:19.560
Senpai!

00:04:19.560 --> 00:04:20.980
Good luck!

00:04:23.910 --> 00:04:27.320
<i>Sugimoto was tearing up.</i>

00:04:27.320 --> 00:04:28.950
<i>In fact, he was crying.</i>

00:04:30.040 --> 00:04:32.840
<i>I was in the feed zone last 
year and the year before.</i>

00:04:32.840 --> 00:04:35.060
<i>I know what it's like</i>

00:04:35.950 --> 00:04:38.960
<i>to wait and wait for your team to come.</i>

00:04:39.490 --> 00:04:42.880
<i>It makes you want to cry, but...</i>

00:04:43.820 --> 00:04:47.590
<i>This time, I have to do something 
about this situation.</i>

00:04:48.510 --> 00:04:50.620
<i>But how?</i>

00:04:55.350 --> 00:04:59.400
You must be slow if you're 
still hanging around here.

00:04:59.990 --> 00:05:03.440
This year's Sohoku team sure is slow.

00:05:04.730 --> 00:05:06.970
<i>Pursuers? You can't be serious.</i>

00:05:06.970 --> 00:05:08.810
<i>They caught up to us from behind?</i>

00:05:09.950 --> 00:05:12.200
You're slower than last year.

00:05:12.200 --> 00:05:14.710
Higo blooms again!

00:05:15.130 --> 00:05:16.820
<i>Kumamoto Daiichi?</i>

00:05:19.420 --> 00:05:21.810
We trained for the flats 
on the plains of Kumamoto

00:05:21.810 --> 00:05:24.770
and polished our climbing 
on the slopes of Mt. Aso.

00:05:24.770 --> 00:05:31.170
We are the Kumamoto Daiichi 
Higo Superexpress!

00:05:31.170 --> 00:05:33.270
<i>Kumamoto Daiichi third-year Ise!</i>

00:05:33.270 --> 00:05:39.440
We let Kyoto and Hakone take the sprint 
and deliberately left the pack late.

00:05:40.450 --> 00:05:45.540
If we'd left early, we would've 
ended up like you, in pieces!

00:05:47.370 --> 00:05:50.060
This year's Kumamoto Daiichi is smart.

00:05:50.060 --> 00:05:55.540
We planned to delay our move and chase after 
the front with all six of our members.

00:05:56.250 --> 00:05:57.630
<i>The front?</i>

00:05:58.420 --> 00:06:02.090
<i>They're heading for the 
front? In that case...</i>

00:06:02.460 --> 00:06:04.960
E-Excuse me, Ise-san...

00:06:04.960 --> 00:06:10.090
You rode with a very energetic guy 
named Taura-san last year, didn't you?

00:06:10.740 --> 00:06:13.740
Are you trying to say we've changed,

00:06:14.130 --> 00:06:16.430
tag #1, Onoda-kun?

00:06:17.830 --> 00:06:22.390
Oh, no! Um, I'm sorry if I offended you!

00:06:22.390 --> 00:06:24.020
You're right.

00:06:24.750 --> 00:06:28.150
I took over the club after Taura-san.

00:06:28.820 --> 00:06:34.870
I don't want to face the pain we experienced 
last year again, so I've become a demon.

00:06:35.350 --> 00:06:40.490
The underclassmen call me the Demon Sergeant!

00:06:41.330 --> 00:06:42.490
Ise!

00:06:44.490 --> 00:06:47.790
Why don't we work together 
until we reach the front?

00:06:48.990 --> 00:06:50.630
Us and Kumamoto Daiichi...

00:06:51.690 --> 00:06:57.100
In a road race, the more people there 
are in a group, the faster they go!

00:06:58.540 --> 00:07:00.770
Not a bad deal, right?

00:07:03.310 --> 00:07:08.180
Didn't I mention last 
year's painful experience?

00:07:08.180 --> 00:07:12.360
We're done with cooperating!

00:07:12.990 --> 00:07:14.370
<i>That's right.</i>

00:07:14.370 --> 00:07:18.620
<i>Last year, during the third day's 
final stage, Kumamoto Daiichi</i>

00:07:18.940 --> 00:07:21.650
<i>was abandoned by the guys from Hiroshima.</i>

00:07:26.020 --> 00:07:29.260
I've got another piece of bad news for you.

00:07:30.300 --> 00:07:34.300
The pack behind us is slowly gaining speed.

00:07:34.730 --> 00:07:37.930
If you keep riding at that pace,

00:07:38.790 --> 00:07:42.310
forget about the front—the pack 
behind will catch up to you.

00:07:45.470 --> 00:07:47.330
How could we have fallen so far behind?

00:07:48.100 --> 00:07:51.650
It's because I made the wrong choice.

00:07:52.260 --> 00:07:54.470
<i>Forget about the front 
because of the pack behind...</i>

00:07:55.130 --> 00:07:59.200
<i>I didn't plan on giving up,</i>

00:07:59.930 --> 00:08:04.910
<i>but should we leave Naruko alone and...</i>

00:08:06.350 --> 00:08:07.590
Captain Ise!

00:08:07.590 --> 00:08:10.550
The pursuers behind us 
have fallen out of sight!

00:08:10.550 --> 00:08:12.420
We've shaken off Sohoku!

00:08:12.770 --> 00:08:14.500
Roger that.

00:08:14.500 --> 00:08:18.770
They were as persistent this 
year as they were last year.

00:08:18.770 --> 00:08:21.100
Sohoku's impressive.

00:08:21.490 --> 00:08:23.740
But their race is over now.

00:08:24.290 --> 00:08:28.400
Kumamoto Daiichi finished them off.

00:08:28.800 --> 00:08:33.040
Since they're not trying to catch up, 
they must've lost the will to fight.

00:08:33.040 --> 00:08:34.660
They've given up

00:08:36.500 --> 00:08:38.370
on this race!

00:08:49.820 --> 00:08:51.960
<i>What's going on? Onoda?</i>

00:08:52.770 --> 00:08:56.050
<i>What is this rising pressure?</i>

00:08:56.790 --> 00:08:58.130
<i>Onoda?</i>

00:08:58.820 --> 00:09:00.390
<i>Despite the circumstances,</i>

00:09:01.730 --> 00:09:03.070
<i>he's smiling?</i>

00:09:05.620 --> 00:09:07.130
What's up, Onoda?

00:09:07.750 --> 00:09:09.650
Uh, sorry.

00:09:10.290 --> 00:09:13.370
I know I shouldn't be smiling.

00:09:13.950 --> 00:09:16.410
I just couldn't help but imagine...

00:09:17.430 --> 00:09:21.150
Kumamoto Daiichi said the 
pack is close behind us.

00:09:21.950 --> 00:09:29.540
The board on the referee car just said 
there's two guys riding ahead of the pack.

00:09:30.310 --> 00:09:33.380
I thought it might be possible that

00:09:34.370 --> 00:09:39.720
Aoyagi-san and Kaburagi-kun will 
catch up and ride with us again.

00:09:40.470 --> 00:09:43.720
I'm sure we'll be faster 
when there's five of us.

00:09:45.730 --> 00:09:47.980
<i>Aoyagi-san and Kaburagi?</i>

00:09:48.700 --> 00:09:50.980
<i>They could catch up?</i>

00:09:51.610 --> 00:09:54.360
Faster with five?

00:09:54.360 --> 00:09:56.400
Yeah.

00:09:56.400 --> 00:09:58.780
But it's still just my imagination.

00:09:59.410 --> 00:10:03.980
<i>Since we've fallen behind the front, 
it means we're closer to the back.</i>

00:10:04.710 --> 00:10:06.390
<i>I hadn't even considered that.</i>

00:10:08.180 --> 00:10:10.100
<i>I hadn't considered that 
we'd increased our odds of</i>

00:10:10.100 --> 00:10:12.060
<i>grouping up with our teammates behind us.</i>

00:10:13.410 --> 00:10:16.410
B-But it's not guaranteed!

00:10:16.410 --> 00:10:18.940
It's just a possibility!

00:10:20.090 --> 00:10:23.930
<i>We can ride with Kaburagi and Aoyagi again.</i>

00:10:29.750 --> 00:10:32.740
<i>No. We're in the middle of a race.</i>

00:10:32.740 --> 00:10:34.690
<i>And I'm the captain.</i>

00:10:35.660 --> 00:10:37.500
That's not happening, Onoda.

00:10:37.910 --> 00:10:39.780
Kumamoto Daiichi passed us,

00:10:40.290 --> 00:10:44.150
but we're still chasing after the lead pack.

00:10:45.230 --> 00:10:46.620
And I...

00:10:47.550 --> 00:10:49.870
have abandoned them!

00:10:50.450 --> 00:10:53.250
Then this is goodbye.

00:10:53.940 --> 00:10:55.490
They're not coming.

00:10:55.970 --> 00:10:59.090
We won't slow down to wait for them, either.

00:10:59.700 --> 00:11:00.930
Don't look back.

00:11:00.930 --> 00:11:03.300
We'll catch up to the front.

00:11:03.300 --> 00:11:05.140
We'll chase after them as quickly as we can.

00:11:05.140 --> 00:11:08.890
That's an order! Pedal as hard as you can!

00:11:08.890 --> 00:11:12.840
We must catch up to Hakone Academy
 and Kyoto Fushimi!

00:11:12.840 --> 00:11:14.150
Yes, sir!

00:11:17.300 --> 00:11:20.360
<i>Onoda's smiling again?</i>

00:11:20.820 --> 00:11:22.180
Onoda, let's switch!

00:11:22.180 --> 00:11:24.060
Th-Thank you.

00:11:25.830 --> 00:11:27.950
What's going on, Onoda?

00:11:28.990 --> 00:11:30.780
Why are you smiling?

00:11:30.780 --> 00:11:33.110
Has the heat made you lose your mind?

00:11:33.110 --> 00:11:35.750
I said we're chasing after 
the front at full speed.

00:11:36.830 --> 00:11:37.710
Yes, sir.

00:11:38.750 --> 00:11:44.300
Oh, um... Aoyagi-san promised he'd be back.

00:11:45.140 --> 00:11:46.810
I'm bringing him back.

00:11:47.890 --> 00:11:51.140
Teshima-san, you said the 
eighth reason was hope.

00:11:51.140 --> 00:11:56.150
Those seven more reasons my choice 
is reckless... Is there an eighth?

00:11:56.150 --> 00:11:58.480
What? The eighth?

00:11:58.480 --> 00:12:00.280
There's...

00:12:01.140 --> 00:12:03.280
It's a tiny shred of hope!

00:12:04.890 --> 00:12:07.870
You didn't need to remember that.

00:12:07.870 --> 00:12:12.120
I think they've broken through the seven 
obstacles and are headed this way.

00:12:13.510 --> 00:12:17.000
Sorry, but that's too optimistic.

00:12:17.000 --> 00:12:20.110
We're heading for the front 
as quickly as we can.

00:12:21.290 --> 00:12:23.010
How will they catch up?

00:12:23.730 --> 00:12:26.460
The mountains were probably hard for them.

00:12:27.020 --> 00:12:28.390
But this course

00:12:29.310 --> 00:12:34.190
has been a gently sloping downhill 
since we exited the tunnel.

00:12:35.180 --> 00:12:38.230
I'm sure they'll catch up.

00:12:38.230 --> 00:12:39.690
After all,

00:12:40.590 --> 00:12:42.490
they're sprinters.

00:12:48.830 --> 00:12:49.580
Aoyagi-san...

00:12:50.530 --> 00:12:51.620
What is it?

00:12:54.570 --> 00:12:56.740
They're faster than the 
guys we've seen so far.

00:12:56.740 --> 00:12:59.140
The wind was making the leaves shake.

00:12:59.810 --> 00:13:02.050
They're the guys who competed 
for yesterday's sprint.

00:13:02.550 --> 00:13:08.230
I can hear the fans saying we're fast,
 but this is normal, right?

00:13:08.740 --> 00:13:12.050
I'm an all-rounder, not a sprinter.

00:13:12.730 --> 00:13:13.640
You're right.

00:13:21.630 --> 00:13:24.150
<i>No, stay strong.</i>

00:13:24.150 --> 00:13:27.070
<i>Putting your hopes in the guys behind 
you is proof you're wavering.</i>

00:13:27.940 --> 00:13:29.950
<i>Don't turn back, Teshima Junta.</i>

00:13:30.540 --> 00:13:32.240
<i>Aoyagi is a good guy.</i>

00:13:32.240 --> 00:13:35.410
<i>We've fought and eaten 
together for three years.</i>

00:13:36.030 --> 00:13:38.080
Pick up the pace!

00:13:38.970 --> 00:13:42.750
<i>Earnest, silent, and 
considerate of his juniors...</i>

00:13:43.500 --> 00:13:45.400
<i>But I've abandoned him!</i>

00:13:45.400 --> 00:13:47.180
<i>He's not coming!</i>

00:13:48.150 --> 00:13:49.930
Let's go faster!

00:13:50.430 --> 00:13:52.590
It's the three-man Sohoku team!

00:13:52.590 --> 00:13:54.140
You can do it!

00:13:55.270 --> 00:13:56.990
Some guys are coming from behind!

00:13:56.990 --> 00:13:57.890
There's two of them!

00:13:59.020 --> 00:14:00.400
<i>Two?</i>

00:14:01.170 --> 00:14:03.770
<i>No, it's some other team.</i>

00:14:04.220 --> 00:14:06.700
<i>They're chasing after us 
like Kumamoto Daiichi did.</i>

00:14:07.470 --> 00:14:10.410
<i>Don't turn back, Teshima Junta!</i>

00:14:18.020 --> 00:14:20.930
<i>I can't let them catch up to us!</i>

00:14:21.470 --> 00:14:22.880
Teshima-san!

00:14:23.910 --> 00:14:26.170
Behind us! Look behind us!

00:14:28.270 --> 00:14:32.140
<i>Wishes made so long ago...</i>

00:14:33.300 --> 00:14:35.140
<i>sometimes come true.</i>

00:14:39.270 --> 00:14:40.850
It's finally over.

00:14:40.850 --> 00:14:44.040
Laundry, cleanup,
 and prepping for tomorrow...

00:14:44.040 --> 00:14:47.360
Working support for the Inter-High 
is harder than I thought.

00:14:48.740 --> 00:14:50.700
Being a first-year is hard.

00:14:50.700 --> 00:14:51.990
Yeah.

00:14:53.070 --> 00:14:54.660
But Aoyagi...

00:14:55.810 --> 00:14:58.430
Someday, let's race in the Inter-High.

00:14:59.790 --> 00:15:01.710
Let's compete on the ultimate stage.

00:15:02.980 --> 00:15:05.590
Let's do it by the time we're third-years.

00:15:06.620 --> 00:15:10.020
I'll be a climber, and you'll be a sprinter.

00:15:10.430 --> 00:15:11.680
Just kidding.

00:15:12.630 --> 00:15:15.310
When the time comes, 
I'll pull you to the mountains.

00:15:24.270 --> 00:15:25.440
I'm counting on you.

00:15:26.570 --> 00:15:27.260
Yeah.

00:15:33.550 --> 00:15:35.280
<i>Our small wish...</i>

00:15:40.140 --> 00:15:42.200
Onoda, are those...

00:15:42.200 --> 00:15:44.580
Yes. They're yellow jerseys.

00:15:46.050 --> 00:15:51.800
I'd given up hope long ago, but...

00:15:52.930 --> 00:15:56.810
Why do you always come

00:15:57.930 --> 00:16:02.510
to save me only when I'm in trouble?

00:16:04.690 --> 00:16:05.930
You idiot!

00:16:07.140 --> 00:16:09.230
Aoyagi!

00:16:12.260 --> 00:16:15.340
I brought the idiot back again, Junta.

00:16:18.070 --> 00:16:23.250
<i>So casually, and without a 
single change in expression...</i>

00:16:23.970 --> 00:16:27.920
<i>How can you be there like that?</i>

00:16:28.810 --> 00:16:30.430
I see them, Onoda.

00:16:31.290 --> 00:16:32.420
I see them, too.

00:16:35.070 --> 00:16:41.010
The teammates I thought 
would never come back.

00:16:42.250 --> 00:16:43.940
We're here, Aoyagi-san.

00:16:44.740 --> 00:16:46.590
Three yellow jerseys.

00:16:46.590 --> 00:16:48.820
We're almost to our team.

00:16:49.170 --> 00:16:52.150
It's Onoda-san, Imaizumi-san, 
and Teshima-san.

00:16:52.770 --> 00:16:55.780
This is crazy. It feels 
like it's been so long.

00:16:55.780 --> 00:16:57.030
We're almost there.

00:17:03.350 --> 00:17:04.390
<i>Aoyagi...</i>

00:17:06.510 --> 00:17:08.590
<i>That shred of hope...</i>

00:17:09.570 --> 00:17:12.210
<i>The tiny wish I mentioned then...</i>

00:17:12.850 --> 00:17:14.090
<i>Those wishes...</i>

00:17:15.100 --> 00:17:19.770
<i>As we're struggling, they suddenly come true.</i>

00:17:20.490 --> 00:17:22.600
<i>That's how it is.</i>

00:17:24.300 --> 00:17:29.490
<i>I met you the day I was 
thinking about quitting cycling.</i>

00:17:30.150 --> 00:17:32.480
..."one" for number one.

00:17:33.230 --> 00:17:36.950
<i>I failed to make it to the Inter-High,
 but you charmed me.</i>

00:17:37.420 --> 00:17:42.200
<i>When I had lost hope, you asked me
 if I wanted to be your partner.</i>

00:17:43.950 --> 00:17:45.660
We're a two-man team.

00:17:47.180 --> 00:17:49.230
<i>During our second-year training camp,</i>

00:17:49.230 --> 00:17:52.960
<i>when I had given up hope, 
you told me to keep riding.</i>

00:17:53.940 --> 00:17:55.220
We'll go together.

00:17:56.980 --> 00:17:59.260
Otherwise, there's no point.

00:18:00.230 --> 00:18:02.310
<i>During this year's training camp,</i>

00:18:02.310 --> 00:18:06.410
<i>in the final sprint of my race against Koga,</i>

00:18:07.300 --> 00:18:09.650
<i>you were the only one who believed in me.</i>

00:18:10.230 --> 00:18:12.410
Junta, win!

00:18:13.420 --> 00:18:16.820
<i>And now, you promised you'd return.</i>

00:18:17.550 --> 00:18:21.190
<i>You actually left the team and returned</i>

00:18:22.730 --> 00:18:25.330
<i>with our teammate in tow.</i>

00:18:29.020 --> 00:18:30.190
<i>Aoyagi...</i>

00:18:31.580 --> 00:18:35.960
<i>Our two-man team...</i>

00:18:35.960 --> 00:18:39.950
<i>can still ride at this Inter-High!</i>

00:18:46.950 --> 00:18:51.400
Kaburagi-kun and Aoyagi-san 
have just rejoined the team!

00:18:51.400 --> 00:18:52.560
Sorry we're late!

00:18:53.050 --> 00:18:55.150
How have you been, Kaburagi?

00:18:55.150 --> 00:18:56.340
Good, sir!

00:18:56.340 --> 00:18:57.820
Well done making it back!

00:18:58.900 --> 00:19:01.450
You shouldn't have fallen 
behind if you're feeling good!

00:19:01.450 --> 00:19:02.570
Sorry!

00:19:03.710 --> 00:19:08.080
<i>In this precarious situation, 
we got five of our members together.</i>

00:19:09.190 --> 00:19:11.220
<i>Just like Onoda said.</i>

00:19:12.820 --> 00:19:13.670
Koga did?

00:19:14.160 --> 00:19:16.060
He waited for me

00:19:16.510 --> 00:19:19.800
and pushed my back during the climb.

00:19:20.780 --> 00:19:22.070
I was really grateful.

00:19:23.750 --> 00:19:27.130
But you're most grateful 
to Aoyagi-san, right?

00:19:27.900 --> 00:19:29.440
What are you talking about?

00:19:29.440 --> 00:19:32.520
Aoyagi fell behind, like me.

00:19:32.520 --> 00:19:35.190
We had no choice but to work together.

00:19:35.860 --> 00:19:40.950
Aoyagi-san left the team by himself 
so he could go back and save you.

00:19:42.290 --> 00:19:43.240
Huh?

00:19:43.660 --> 00:19:48.370
Teshima-san tried to stop him, but he 
promised to bring you back and left.

00:19:48.790 --> 00:19:52.120
A-Are you being serious?

00:19:55.070 --> 00:19:58.420
So follow me. Don't fall behind.

00:19:59.530 --> 00:20:01.840
Seriously?

00:20:02.260 --> 00:20:03.300
Yeah.

00:20:03.940 --> 00:20:07.460
Wh-Why didn't you say so?

00:20:07.460 --> 00:20:08.790
I told you a bunch of times.

00:20:10.810 --> 00:20:13.310
Th-Th-Th-Th-Th-Then...

00:20:16.500 --> 00:20:18.650
I owe you the most!

00:20:19.410 --> 00:20:20.150
Yeah.

00:20:23.140 --> 00:20:25.930
You just noticed, Kaburagi-kun?

00:20:25.930 --> 00:20:27.010
Huh?

00:20:27.930 --> 00:20:31.490
I said some pretty rude things, didn't I?

00:20:31.490 --> 00:20:32.540
Yeah.

00:20:33.550 --> 00:20:36.670
Then I'm the most sorry to you!

00:20:47.670 --> 00:20:49.970
I'm back, Junta!

00:20:51.300 --> 00:20:56.980
Yeah! Somewhere in my heart,
 I believed this would happen, Aoyagi!

00:20:57.570 --> 00:20:59.980
Thanks for coming back!

00:21:01.030 --> 00:21:02.240
There's five of us.

00:21:02.910 --> 00:21:06.790
Kyoto Fushimi, Hakone Academy, and 
Kumamoto Daiichi are ahead of us.

00:21:06.790 --> 00:21:09.230
Naruko's working hard on his own.

00:21:09.810 --> 00:21:11.810
Sprinters to the front!

00:21:11.810 --> 00:21:14.080
Sohoku is accelerating!

00:21:14.080 --> 00:21:17.000
We'll work together and
 catch up to the lead pack!

00:21:17.610 --> 00:21:18.250
Yes, sir!

00:21:19.030 --> 00:21:20.130
Yes, sir!

00:21:21.870 --> 00:21:22.920
<i>We're going!</i>

00:21:23.710 --> 00:21:25.250
<i>To the front!</i>

00:21:29.420 --> 00:21:32.600
<i>Once these flats end, 
we'll be in the mountains.</i>

00:21:36.150 --> 00:21:38.780
You'll come, won't you, Sakamichi-kun?

00:23:14.500 --> 00:23:18.090
For a minute there,
 I thought we were done for.

00:23:18.500 --> 00:23:20.750
Aoyagi-san, I'm seriously 
most grateful to you.

00:23:21.200 --> 00:23:23.250
Then you can't be rude to him anymore.

00:23:23.250 --> 00:23:26.070
Yes, sir. Sorry, Aoyagi-san.

00:23:27.220 --> 00:23:29.670
How did you and Aoyagi-san
 make it back here?

00:23:29.670 --> 00:23:31.250
Well...

00:23:31.250 --> 00:23:33.250
I-It's a secret!

00:23:33.250 --> 00:23:34.610
Together we sang <i>Love</i>—

00:23:34.610 --> 00:23:35.660
Aoyagi!

00:23:36.030 --> 00:23:39.930
<i>NEXT LINE  Start of the Mountains</i>

00:23:36.850 --> 00:23:38.330
I prefer not using honorifics, after all.

00:23:39.930 --> 00:23:44.940
This is a work of fiction. All characters and organizations
 appearing in this work are fictional. In this work,
 characters sometimes engage in dangerous activities.
 While riding bicycles on actual roads,
 please follow all traffic laws and ride safely.

00:23:44.940 --> 00:23:51.000
<b>Don't miss the next episode</b>
